                        <li class="list-item">
                            <span class="bold-text">Preference for
                                Depth:</span> Low extraversion individuals
                            tend to
                            prioritize deep, meaningful
                            connections over superficial interactions. They
                            may have a small circle of close friends
                            with whom they share deep bonds and intimate
                            conversations.
                        </li>
                        <li class="list-item">
                            <span class="bold-text">Reserved Expression of
                                Emotions:</span> People low in extraversion
                            may be less expressive in
                            their emotions, preferring to keep their
                            feelings and thoughts private rather than
                            sharing them openly with others. They may
                            require more time and trust to feel
                            comfortable expressing themselves fully.
                        </li>
                        <li class="list-item">
                            <span class="bold-text">Preference for Quiet
                                Environments:</span> Low extraversion
                            individuals may be more
                            sensitive to overstimulating environments and
                            may prefer quiet, peaceful surroundings
                            where they can focus and recharge. They may feel
                            drained or overwhelmed by noisy or
                            crowded environments.
                        </li>
                        <li class="list-item">
