                            relationships. They may invest deeply in a few
                            close friendships rather than
                            maintaining a wide network of acquaintances.
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>
                        Overall, low extraversion is associated with traits
                        such as introversion, introspection,
                        independence, and selectivity in social
                        interactions. While they may not seek out social
                        stimulation as frequently as their extraverted
                        counterparts, individuals low in
                        extraversion can still form deep and meaningful
                        connections with others and find
                        fulfillment in their own unique ways.
                    </p>
