            <section>
                <div>
                    <h3 class="vertical-space">
                        Agreeableness
                    </h3>
                    <p>
                        Agreeableness refers to the extent to which
                        individuals are compassionate, cooperative,
                        trusting, and considerate in their interactions with
                        others.
                    </p>
                    <p class="top-extra-space">
                        Individuals who score <span class="bold-text">high
                            in agreeableness</span> exhibit several
                        characteristic traits and
                        behaviors that distinguish them from those who score
                        lower on this personality
                        dimension.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Here are some key aspects of people high in
                        agreeableness:
                    </p>
                    <ul>
                        <li class="list-item">
                            <span class="bold-text">Warmth and
                                Compassion:</span> Agreeable individuals are
                            known for
                            their warmth and
                            compassion towards others. They genuinely care
                            about the well-being of those around
                            them and are quick to offer support,
                            encouragement, and empathy.
                        </li>
                        <li class="list-item">
                            <span class="bold-text">Cooperation and
                                Collaboration:</span> People high in
                            agreeableness
                            value cooperation and
                            collaboration in their interactions with others.
                            They are team players who strive to
                            maintain harmonious relationships and work
                            towards common goals with kindness and
                            understanding.
                        </li>
                        <li class="list-item">
                            <span class="bold-text">Empathy and
                                Sensitivity:</span> Agreeable individuals
                            are highly
                            attuned to the emotions and
                            needs of others. They possess a strong sense of
                            empathy and sensitivity, making them
                            adept at recognizing and responding to the
                            feelings of those around them.
                        </li>
                        <li class="list-item">
                            <span class="bold-text">Conflict
                                Avoidance:</span> Individuals high in
                            agreeableness tend to
                            avoid confrontation and
                            conflict whenever possible. They prioritize
                            harmony and peace in their relationships
                            and may go to great lengths to resolve
                            disagreements in a diplomatic and amicable
                            manner.
                        </li>
                        <li class="list-item">
                            <span class="bold-text">Trust and
                                Cooperation:</span> Agreeable individuals
                            are trusting and
                            optimistic in their
                            interactions with others. They believe in the
                            inherent goodness of people and are
                            willing to extend trust and cooperation, even to
                            those they may not know well.
                        </li>
                        <li class="list-item">
                            <span class="bold-text">Altruism and
                                Generosity:</span> People high in
                            agreeableness are
                            often characterized by
                            their altruistic tendencies and generosity
                            towards others. They derive satisfaction from
                            helping and supporting those in need, often
                            going out of their way to make a positive
                            difference in the lives of others.
                        </li>
                        <li class="list-item">
                            <span class="bold-text">Tolerance and
                                Flexibility:</span> Agreeable individuals
                            are
                            open-minded and tolerant of
                            differing perspectives and beliefs. They embrace
                            diversity and seek to understand and
                            appreciate the unique qualities and experiences
                            of those around them.
                        </li>
                        <li class="list-item">
                            <span class="bold-text">Conflict Resolution
                                Skills:</span> Individuals high in
                            agreeableness
                            excel in conflict resolution
                            and negotiation. They are skilled at finding
                            common ground and facilitating
                            compromise, fostering win-win solutions that
                            benefit all parties involved.
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>
                        Overall, agreeableness is associated with qualities
                        such as warmth, compassion, empathy,
                        and cooperation. Individuals high in agreeableness
                        contribute to positive and harmonious
                        social environments, fostering strong relationships
                        built on trust, understanding, and
                        mutual respect.
                    </p>
                    <p class="top-extra-space">
                        Individuals who score <span class="bold-text">low in
                            agreeableness</span> exhibit certain
                        characteristic traits and
                        behaviors that distinguish them from those who score
                        higher on this personality
                        dimension.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Here are some key aspects of people low in
                        agreeableness:
                    </p>
                    <ul>
                        <li class="list-item">
                            <span class="bold-text">Assertiveness:</span>
                            People low in agreeableness tend to prioritize
                            their own needs and
                            interests over those of others. They may be more
                            assertive and self-focused in their
                            interactions, asserting their opinions and
                            desires without considering the perspectives
                            or feelings of others.
                        </li>
                        <li class="list-item">
                            <span class="bold-text">Competitiveness:</span>
                            Low agreeableness individuals may have a
                            competitive and
                            individualistic mindset, seeking to outperform
                            others and achieve their goals at any cost.
                            They may prioritize personal success and
                            achievement over cooperation and
                            collaboration with others.
                        </li>
                        <li class="list-item">
                            <span class="bold-text">Bluntness and
                                Directness:</span> Individuals low in
                            agreeableness
                            may be more blunt and
                            direct in their communication style, often
                            expressing their opinions and criticisms
                            without sugarcoating or considering the impact
                            on others' feelings. They value honesty
                            and authenticity, even if it comes across as
                            harsh or abrasive.
                        </li>
                        <li class="list-item">
                            <span class="bold-text">Conflict-prone:</span>
                            Low agreeableness individuals may be more
                            prone to conflict and
                            disagreement in their relationships. They may
                            struggle to compromise or find common
                            ground with others, leading to tension and
                            discord in interpersonal interactions.
                        </li>
                        <li class="list-item">
                            <span class="bold-text">Skepticism and
                                Distrust:</span> People low in agreeableness
                            may be
                            skeptical of others'
                            intentions and motivations, viewing the world
                            with a sense of caution and suspicion.
                            They may be less trusting and more guarded in
                            their relationships, preferring to keep
                            their distance from others.
                        </li>
                        <li class="list-item">
                            <span class="bold-text">Self-Reliance:</span>
                            Individuals low in agreeableness value their
                            independence and selfreliance. They may prefer
                            to rely on their own judgment and resources
                            rather than
                            seeking support or assistance from others. They
                            may view dependence on others as a
                            sign of weakness.
                        </li>
                        <li class="list-item">
                            <span class="bold-text">Impersonal
                                Relationships:</span> Low agreeableness
                            individuals may
                            have difficulty forming
                            close, interpersonal connections with others.
                            They may prioritize their own needs and
                            interests above the needs of their
                            relationships, leading to a lack of emotional
                            intimacy
                            and connection.
                        </li>
                        <li class="list-item">
                            <span class="bold-text">Insensitive to Others'
                                Feelings:</span> People low in
                            agreeableness may be less attuned to
                            the emotions and feelings of others. They may
                            have difficulty empathizing with
                            others' experiences and may come across as cold
                            or indifferent in their interactions.
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>
                        Overall, low agreeableness is associated with traits
                        such as assertiveness,
                        competitiveness, bluntness, and skepticism. While
                        individuals low in agreeableness may
                        excel in certain areas such as assertiveness and
                        independence, they may also struggle
                        with interpersonal relationships and cooperation due
                        to their tendency to prioritize
                        their own needs over those of others.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </section>

