                            their ability to overcome obstacles and adapt to
                            changing circumstances.
                        </li>
                        <li class="list-item">
                            <span class="bold-text">Calmness and
                                Composure:</span> Low neuroticism
                            individuals typically
                            maintain a sense of
                            calmness and composure even in the midst of
                            adversity. They are able to keep their
                            emotions in check and respond to stressful
                            situations in a rational and level-headed
                            manner.
                        </li>
                        <li class="list-item">
                            <span class="bold-text">Resilience:</span>
                            People low in neuroticism possess a strong sense
                            of resilience and inner
                            strength. They are able to bounce back quickly
                            from setbacks and disappointments,
                            viewing them as temporary setbacks rather than
                            insurmountable obstacles.
                        </li>
                        <li class="list-item">
                            <span class="bold-text">Steadiness in
                                Relationships:</span> Low neuroticism
                            individuals tend
                            to have stable and
                            harmonious relationships with others. They are
                            less likely to engage in conflict or
                            drama and are able to maintain a sense of
                            equilibrium and harmony in their
